<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<robot name="mc1">
  <!-- MC1 — next-gen robot: the old Codey body with the new 6-DOF CubeMars
     arms. Rebuilt 2026-08-07 (v2).
     * Body (chassis, wheels, legs, torso, neck, head, chest camera,
       5-finger hands) comes from the main-branch Codey model, joint
       names unchanged: knees / hips (mimic) / torso_rotate / neck_turn /
       head_nod / chest_camera / <side>_{thumb,index,middle,ring,pinky}.
     * Arms are the new chain verbatim (its own DH-style frames: every
       joint axis is the local z). They mount on `torso` at the old
       shoulder positions with a 15-degree-up install —
       rpy="0 -1.309 +-1.5707963" is the firmware GravityFF anchor and
       MUST NOT change (nothing between the ground and the arm bases
       rotates them: knees/hips form a level-keeping parallelogram and
       torso_rotate spins about gravity).
     * Hands hang off the arm TCPs (0.075 m past link_6); the old wrist
       joint is gone — the new arm's joint_6 IS the wrist.
     * Sensor frames: laser / imu / 4 downward cliff TOF / 2 bumper
       limit switches / chest_camera_sensor / head_camera_link.
       Camera OPTICAL frames are deliberately absent: the realsense ROS
       driver publishes them on hardware, the Isaac bridge in sim. -->
